  [1mThe main choice: build the page from the vendored Keel kit, not by copying [38;5;153mservices.js[39m.[0m The kit in [38;5;153mvendor/kit/[39m already
  has the pieces the page needs: a page header, the environment dropdown, a sortable table, colored chips and an
  empty-state message. Its table sorts the rows and builds the sort links using the same rule as Services: clicking the
  active column flips it, and any other column starts ascending. It also changes the page on the dropdown and keeps the
  sort when the filter changes, so you get the same behavior with much less code.

  [1mThe plan has two tasks:[0m
  1. [1mThe page itself[0m ([38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m), with 9 tests. They cover the filter, both sorts, the chip colors, the
     duration format, the empty state, and unknown query values falling back to the defaults.
  2. [1mThe route, the nav link after "Services", and a README line[0m, plus server tests for the route and its 503 page. The
     existing 503 "Snapshot unavailable" handling covers the new snapshot without any change.

